+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ARD1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "One of three geographically and petrologically related centres forming the Ardnamurchan peninsula, together comprising the Ardnamurchan Central Complex (ARDNA)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ARD2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "One of three geographically and petrologically related centres forming the Ardnamurchan peninsula, together comprising the Ardnamurchan Central Complex (ARDNA)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ARD3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "One of three geographically and petrologically related centres forming the Ardnamurchan peninsula, together comprising the Ardnamurchan Central Complex (ARDNA)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ARDNA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A component of the Hebridean Province comprising three geographically and petrologically related centres (Ardnamurchan Centre 1 (ARD1), Ardnamurchan Centre 2 (ARD2), and Ardnamurchan Centre 3 (ARD3)) forming the Ardnamurchan peninsula. Includes a wide variety of intrusive and extrusive igneous rocks, together with both sedimentary and metamorphic country rocks, particularly in major vent-complexes."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BDH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Limestone."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/C2IB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Numerous basic cone-sheets, mainly porphyritic dolerite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/C2OB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Numerous basic cone-sheets, mainly quartz-dolerite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/C3B> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A few basic cone-sheets. Basalt, and dolerite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/C3OGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-glomerocrystic gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CECH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Volcaniclastic rocks with trace basalt and bytownite gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRUG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Limestone."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUIL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, peridotite, granite. Also intrusion-breccia, tuffisite and volcaniclastic-breccia."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUIL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Bytownite gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUIL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Bytownite gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HBFZ> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "The Highland Boundary Fault Zone comprises a mix of fault breccia and cataclasite with locally complex associations with rocks of the Highland Border Complex including serpentinites and ophicarbonates. Later dolerite dykes have intruded along parts of the fault zone."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MNCND> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Microgranite, quartz-dolerite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MULL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Several basaltic lavas and beds of volcaniclastic sedimentary rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SMQD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Quartz-dolerite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SNCC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granophyric granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WBFZ> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Cataclasite and mylonite with trace metalimestone, pelite, psammite and quartzite."@en .
